r_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"e0ccfb99cc37827995039d5a0a031a8321c211c0038d6af0c5c461daaf9bfbe1","event_uuid":"e556d143-5c21-4a7a-8a1e-53ade110f4b6","position":{"commit_sha":"6864af5f5bb34f54fafcd5ed555b1c7c649de436","position":"1786508365753892218-e556d143-5c21-4a7a-8a1e-53ade110f4b6"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-227_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"6f8df6b5-44f6-4ea4-b224-1eac4c95b0a7","comments":[],"created_at":1786383846571877001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"e563df87-725f-4420-8586-5c0a019f250d","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"2923-8b46-c022-46ce"},{"link_uuid":"e556d143-5c21-4a7a-8a1e-53ade110f4b6","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"02e3-1aae-13d4-4159"}],"description":"# A gate run does not notice its own binary is older than the base ref it pins\n\n`review-plan` (and every other code-reading gate) snapshots the base ref's tree into\n`/tmp/rebar-gate-snapshots/<sha>/` and reviews against it, but nothing compares the\nRUNNING BUILD to that sha. A checkout that has drifted behind `origin/main` silently\nreviews new material with old code.\n\n## Observed\n\nThree consecutive `review-plan` runs were executed from `~/rebar/.venv` — a legitimate\nrepo checkout venv, which is what AGENTS.md asks for — while that checkout sat 24 commits\nbehind `origin/main`. The only symptom was one easily-missed line:\n\n    WARNING rebar.config: rebar config (/tmp/rebar-gate-snapshots/2bce1407.../rebar.toml):\n    unknown key 'verify.suggest_duplicate_tickets' ignored (typo? see docs/config.md)\n\nThat key is not a typo. Commit 74a7332606 (\"9416: rename overlap_enabled for what it\ndoes\") renamed `verify.overlap_enabled` -> `verify.suggest_duplicate_tickets`. The stale\nbuild predates the rename, so it read the CURRENT base ref's config, did not recognise the\ncurrent key name, and silently ignored the operator's setting.\n\n## Scope\n\nOperator decision (2026-08-12): this ticket covers the build-drift warning only. The\nfourth criterion of the original report — surfacing repeated non-fatal LLM step failures\nin run summaries — is split out to `eclectic-industrial-argali` (61a1-ee49-3c42-4b09),\nlinked `discovered_from`.\n\n## Design\n\nAll code-reading gates converge on `rebar.llm.gate_source.resolve_gate_handle`, which\nresolves the base ref to a pinned sha and acquires the snapshot handle. That is the one\nseam where a drift check belongs.\n\nThe running build's commit is already resolvable: `rebar.signing._gate_commit_sha()`\nreturns the live rebar source checkout's short sha, falling back to the build-baked\n`rebar._build_info.COMMIT` (written by `hatch_build.py`) for wheel installs, and `None`\nwhen neither exists.\n\nDrift = the running build's commit is a strict ancestor of the pinned sha, measured in\nthe target repo. When the gate code and the target repo are different repositories the\nbuild sha simply is not present in the target repo, so the check finds nothing and stays\nsilent — which is the correct behaviour, since drift is only meaningful when rebar is\nreviewing rebar.\n\nThe warning is advisory: reviewing from a slightly-behind checkout is legitimate, so this\nmust never fail a run, never alter a verdict, and never change signing or provenance.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1 — When the running build's commit is a strict ancestor of the sha a gate pins,\n      the gate emits ONE warning naming the build sha, the build commit's date, the pinned\n      sha, and the drift count in commits. It does NOT fail and does NOT alter the verdict,\n      exit code, signature, or provenance stamp.\n- [ ] AC2 — The warning is emitted at most once per (build sha, pinned sha) pair per\n      process, so a run that resolves the handle more than once does not produce a warning\n      storm.\n- [ ] AC3 — When build provenance is unavailable or drift cannot be established, the gate\n      is SILENT: no warning when `_gate_commit_sha()` returns `None`, when the build sha is\n      not present in the target repo (gate code and target are different repos), when the\n      pinned sha is unknown, when git is unavailable, or when the build is at or ahead of\n      the pinned sha.\n- [ ] AC4 — An unknown key in a config snapshot is reported differently when the running\n      build is known to be behind the pinned ref: 'unknown key X (this build may predate\n      it; see docs/config.md)' instead of the 'typo?' wording, which actively misdirects.\n      The default wording is unchanged when no drift was detected.\n- [ ] AC5 — Held-out unit tests cover: behind -> warns once; at/ahead -> silent; provenance\n      unavailable -> silent; build sha absent from the target repo -> silent; and the\n      config unknown-key wording in both the drifted and undrifted states.\n- [ ] AC6 — `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and the unit + interfaces suites pass; every\n      touched file stays under the 800-LOC module cap.\n\n## Provenance\n\nFound while re-running plan review for task b2bb during the store/signing remediation.\nRe-running from a worktree venv at origin/main is the workaround.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/build_drift.py","reason":"new: resolve the running build sha, compare it to the gate-pinned sha, emit the once-per-pair drift warning, and expose the drifted state"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/gate_source.py","reason":"call the drift check from resolve_gate_handle, the seam every code-reading gate converges on"},{"path":"src/rebar/_config_schema.py","reason":"reword the unknown-key warning to (this build may predate it) when drift was detected"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_build_drift.py","reason":"new: held-out tests for behind/at/ahead, missing provenance, foreign repo, once-per-pair, and both config wordings"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","02e3-1aae-13d4-4159"],["relates_to","2923-8b46-c022-46ce"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"303066a5-72e7-48b7-959c-ade8cd7ff0da","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"b273-e0ba-f719-4f1c","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Gate runs do not warn when the running build is behind the base ref","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["2334686a-e711-4e8e-bec0-b35f4e73ff4c","cb9f079f-378c-4666-a79e-ccd5238183c5","75012035-efa6-4905-9bbc-820a48517449","ca2efa79-c288-44f8-9db4-104d36417ce3","303066a5-72e7-48b7-959c-ade8cd7ff0da","2185ec85-ed26-4bfb-95e7-8143ee3b4fe6","e563df87-725f-4420-8586-5c0a019f250d","e556d143-5c21-4a7a-8a1e-53ade110f4b6"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786508365753892219,"uuid":"a2942a25-a7c5-484f-b9a0-66aff183d812"}